        "notes": "All six facts are stated and accurate: the window as a token-counted limit covering everything, the model keeping nothing between calls, history management, cost and context rot despite larger windows, notes saved outside the model and reloaded, and retrieval of only relevant parts. No misconception is asserted. The lesson is well pitched to a junior who has not built an agent, defining token, context window and tool descriptions with the learner's makerspace project, but it is dense for 30 minutes and introduces many terms (parametric memory, just-in-time loading, memory tool commands, RAG), so a few passages stretch the learner."
